<title>AUSTRIA: FRIENDLY COUNTRIES GET PRIORITY IN CONTRACTS-IRAQ.</title>
<headline>FRIENDLY COUNTRIES GET PRIORITY IN CONTRACTS-IRAQ.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraqi oil minister Amir Muhammad Rasheed said on Thursday that &quot;friendly&quot; countries would be given a priority when it comes to award new oil sales contracts under the second phase of the U.N. oil-for-food deal.  </p>
<p>&quot;Friendly countries are definitely a priority when awarding new contracts,&quot; Rasheed told a news briefing.</p>
<p>He named the countries as France, Russia and China.</p>
<p>Rasheed also said that most but not all of those companies awarded contracts under the first tranche would be awarded contracts in the second phase.</p>
<p>He also said the regional pricing mechanism for Iraqi exports from Iraq on the Mediterranean and Mina al-Bakr in the Gulf would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organisation sets price formulas linked to regional benchmarks for Iraqi sales to Asia, Europe, South Africa and the United States.</p>
<p>Rasheed said new pricing formulas for the second phase of exports would be ready a few days after a revised aid distribution plan was in place. The aid plan is expected in 7-10 days, the minister has said.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
